.TH CYCLO-SHOT 1 "August 2026" "Cyclo 0.2.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cyclo-shot \- send a one-shot inference request through a Cyclo Provider
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cyclo-shot
.RI [ options ]
.I model prompt...
.br
.B cyclo-shot
.RI [ options ]
.B --list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cyclo-shot
is a dependency-free operator diagnostic for the outer Provider exposed by a
running Cyclo DComp system. It discovers the loopback-published Provider,
validates the requested model against its catalogue, sends one streaming
inference request, and prints the answer on standard output.
.PP
Unless tracing is disabled, topology, request envelopes, routing metadata,
usage, and component logs emitted during the request are written to standard
error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --list
List available model identifiers and exit.
.TP
.BI --max-tokens\  count
Set the maximum number of output tokens. The default is 256.
.TP
.BI --system\  name
Select a DComp system when more than one Cyclo installation exists.
.TP
.B --no-trace
Print only the model answer.
.TP
.B --json
Write a machine-readable result to standard output and suppress the trace.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cyclo-shot --list
cyclo-shot pool/balanced "reply with exactly: hello"
cyclo-shot --no-trace pool/balanced "tell me a joke"
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 when the Provider emits a terminal error event, and 1
for discovery, transport, protocol, or local execution failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cyclo (1),
.BR docker (1)
